  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Allow users to communicate while their VR headset is temporarily set down.\n\nWhen the headset is on the desk, we can still hear world audio.\n\nKeyboard input already passes through.\n\nThe VRChat desktop window is already running.\n\nHowever, there is no usable way to open the chatbox or control the mic while not looking through the HMD.\n\nThis is not a request to switch to Desktop mode.\n\nMinimal concept:\n\nAdd an optional button in the VRChat desktop window that opens a simple chatbox input field.\n\nThis would allow users to temporarily respond using their keyboard while the headset is off.\n\nAn optional extension could be temporarily selecting a different microphone device in the same window. However, the core request is only basic chat access — mic override is secondary.\n\nNo camera switch.\n\nNo VR/Desktop transition.\n\nNo runtime state changes.\n\nJust minimal communication access while the headset is down.\n\nWhy this matters:\n\nDuring long VR sessions, I sometimes put my headset down for a few minutes but can still hear everything through my PC speakers. If someone talks to me, I currently have no simple way to respond without putting the headset back on, even though I am still present and listening.",
